From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 00:57:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Stamp a restyle hint when remove_node unlinks a child

remove_node marked the parent's ancestors dirty and stamped damage, but
never put a RestyleHint on the parent itself, unlike its sibling
remove_and_drop_node. The traversal therefore reached the parent's
subtree without anything asking for a recascade, so every selector that
reads the parent's child list kept stale style after a removeChild:
:empty, :nth-child and :has all reproduce.

This is the detach-without-drop path, which is what the DOM shim's
removeChild and Element.remove call, so page JS hits it directly.
---
 src/mutator.rs | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mutator.rs b/src/mutator.rs
index 2b169ef..4e15e46 100644
--- a/src/mutator.rs
+++ b/src/mutator.rs
@@ -689,6 +689,17 @@ impl DocumentMutator<'_> {
             self.mutations_occurred |= node_is_in_document;
             let parent = &mut self.doc.nodes[parent_id];
             parent.insert_damage(ALL_DAMAGE);
+
+            // Marking ancestors dirty without stamping a hint leaves
+            // nothing to recascade the parent.
+
+            // Any selector reading the parent's child list (`:empty`,
+            // `:nth-child`, `:has`) would keep stale style after removeChild.
+            if parent.flags.is_in_document() {
+                if let Some(mut data) = parent.try_stylo_element_data_mut().and_then(|s| s.get_mut()) {
+                    data.hint |= RestyleHint::restyle_subtree();
+                }
+            }
             // Mark ancestors dirty so the style traversal visits this subtree.
             parent.mark_ancestors_dirty();
             parent.children.retain(|id| *id != node_id);
